                <invention-title lang="de">CLOUD-PLATTENSPEICHER ZUR UNTERSTÜTZUNG DER VERSCHLÜSSELUNG UND METADATEN AUF DEM PHYSIKALISCHEN FESTPLATTENLAUFWERK</invention-title>
                <invention-title lang="fr">STOCKAGE SUR DISQUE EN NUAGE POUR PRENDRE EN CHARGE UN CHIFFREMENT ET DES MÉTADONNÉES SUR LE LECTEUR DE DISQUE DUR PHYSIQUE</invention-title>
                <invention-title lang="en">CLOUD DISK STORAGE TO SUPPORT ENCRYPTION AND METADATA ON THE PHYSICAL HARD DRIVE</invention-title>
            </bibliographic-data>
            <abstract lang="en">
                <p>A cloud implementation of a persisted storage device, such as a disk, is provided. The implementation supports a variety of features and protocols, in full analogy with a physical storage device such as a disk drive. The present disclosure provides for implementing standard eDrive protocols in the cloud by designing internal disk storage, referred to as a "system area," in a virtual disk instance that the virtual disk can potentially utilize for a multitude of disk features. This internal storage can be used to implement eDrive protocols, which use the system area to maintain the necessary internal virtual disk state.</p>
            </abstract>
